    <artifactId>procedures-service</artifactId>
    <name>Procedures — Clinical Procedures Pipeline platform layer</name>
    <description>
        Clinical-plane platform layer for the Clinical Procedures, Interventions and
        Therapeutic/Diagnostic Actions Pipeline. Owns only capabilities that had no owner:
        the canonical procedure catalogue and its requirements, appropriateness and
        duplication detection, competence and privilege resolution over VARAPI/Vashandi,
        the readiness engine, safety-pause templates, sedation requirement profiles,
        aftercare templates, the procedure execution index and pipeline analytics.

        ENGINE-NOT-STORE. This service evaluates; the executing service persists. Readiness
        verdicts and safety-pause completions are computed here and recorded by whoever runs
        the procedure — inpatient.procedure_readiness_check and procedure_checklist_item stay
        the per-episode record of truth. Two records of one fact is the duplication the
        guardrails forbid, and avoiding it is what makes this service safe to add.

        MUST NOT own: the procedure request record or its fulfilment lifecycle (oros-service,
        order_type=PROCEDURE with the ProcedureWorkflow guard); the procedure execution record,
        specimens, devices, counts or recovery (inpatient-service); consent (mvumo-service);
        terminology (zibo-service); clinical decision logic (clinical-knowledge-platform-service);
        person-level longitudinal clinical registries or the clinical decision that opens or
        closes a phase of care (pct-service, care-continuum-doctrine CC-2).

        See docs/architecture/adr/ADR-SURGERY-AND-PROCEDURES-SERVICE-BOUNDARIES.md.
    </description>

